What Is the Grid Flexibility Aggregation Services Market?
The grid flexibility aggregation services market covers contracted services that coordinate distributed electricity resources, including flexible loads, batteries, electric vehicles and renewable energy assets. Aggregators enrol participants, manage resource availability, coordinate dispatch and verify performance to help utilities and electricity market operators balance supply and demand.

Key Market Drivers
Growing Participation of Distributed Energy Resources
The increasing deployment of residential smart devices, battery storage systems, electric vehicles and controllable industrial loads is expanding the pool of resources available for grid flexibility. Aggregators combine these distributed assets into coordinated portfolios that can provide measurable support to electricity networks.

Expanding Market Access for Aggregated Resources
Regulatory developments and new flexibility procurement programmes are creating additional opportunities for aggregators to participate in wholesale electricity markets and distribution network services. These arrangements support demand for portfolio management, bidding, dispatch coordination and settlement services.

