Market Challenges
Aggregators must coordinate assets with different operating characteristics, communication protocols and availability patterns. Establishing reliable consumption baselines, integrating device telemetry and verifying delivered flexibility can increase technical and operational complexity.

Market Restraints
Customer incentives and equipment costs can reduce the service revenue retained by aggregation providers. Regulatory differences between electricity markets, device interoperability issues and uncertainty in customer response may also limit the scalability of aggregation programmes.

